"domain": [],
"skill": [],
"year": 2019,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 20,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "How many different real numbers \\(x\\) satisfy the equation\n\n\\[ (x^2 - 5)^2 = 16? \\]",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(0\\)",
"B": "\\(1\\)",
"C": "\\(2\\)",
"D": "\\(4\\)",
"E": "\\(8\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "A real number has square \\(16\\) exactly when it is \\(4\\) or \\(-4\\). Apply this to the entire expression \\(x^2-5\\):\n\n\\[\nx^2-5=4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x^2-5=-4.\n\\]\n\nThe first equation gives \\(x^2=9\\), so \\(x=3\\) or \\(-3\\). The second gives \\(x^2=1\\), so \\(x=1\\) or \\(-1\\). These four real numbers are distinct, and the two cases exhaust all possibilities.\n\nThere are \\(\\boxed{4}\\) solutions, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\). Taking a square root of an equation requires keeping both signs.",
"solutionSource": "Adapted from MAA official solutions",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://drive.usercontent.google.com/uc?id=1LNwtmi2U96Fqq23aquyLcXk96BpgcqF4&export=download",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2019/solutions",
