"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 2,
"area": "Prealgebra",
"question": "Four friends do yardwork for their neighbors over the weekend, earning \\(\\$15,\\) \\(\\$20,\\) \\(\\$25,\\) and \\(\\$40\\) respectively. They decide to split their earnings equally among themselves. In total how much will the friend who earned \\(\\$40\\) give to the others?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\$5\\)",
"B": "\\(\\$10\\)",
"C": "\\(\\$15\\)",
"D": "\\(\\$20\\)",
"E": "\\(\\$25\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "An equal split means each friend finishes with one fourth of the total earnings. Together they earned\n\n\\[\n15+20+25+40=100\\text{ dollars},\n\\]\n\nso each person's share is \\(100/4=25\\) dollars.\n\nThe friend who earned \\(40\\) dollars keeps \\(25\\) and gives away \\(40-25=\\boxed{15}\\) dollars, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\). This also fills the other friends' shortfalls of \\(10\\), \\(5\\), and \\(0\\) dollars.",
"solutionSource": "Adapted from MAA official solutions",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://drive.usercontent.google.com/uc?id=1pgLVYoFDn26DYpNrqfrtGWrh0JIpNOgE&export=download",
