"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "A",
"number": 2,
"area": "Prealgebra",
"question": "Portia’s high school has \\(3\\) times as many students as Lara’s high school. The two high schools have a total of \\(2600\\) students. How many students does Portia’s high school have?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(600\\)",
"B": "\\(650\\)",
"C": "\\(1950\\)",
"D": "\\(2000\\)",
"E": "\\(2050\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Lara's school accounts for one equal part and Portia's for three equal parts. Together they account for four parts, so one part contains \\(2600/4=650\\) students.\n\nPortia's school has \\(3\\cdot650=\\boxed{1950}\\) students, choice C. A ratio of \\(3:1\\) means three quarters of the combined total belong to the larger group.",
