"year": 2022,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 10,
"area": "Prealgebra",
"question": "One sunny day, Ling decided to take a hike in the mountains. She left her house at \\(8\\) a.m., drove at a constant speed of \\(45\\) miles per hour, and arrived at the hiking trail at \\(10\\) a.m. After hiking for \\(3\\) hours, Ling drove home at a constant speed of \\(60\\) miles per hour. Which of the following graphs best illustrates the distance between Ling’s car and her house over the course of her trip?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "[Figure 1](figures/2022_AMC_8_Q10_choiceA_fig1.svg)",
"B": "[Figure 2](figures/2022_AMC_8_Q10_choiceB_fig2.svg)",
"C": "[Figure 3](figures/2022_AMC_8_Q10_choiceC_fig3.svg)",
"D": "[Figure 4](figures/2022_AMC_8_Q10_choiceD_fig4.svg)",
"E": "[Figure 5](figures/2022_AMC_8_Q10_choiceE_fig5.svg)"
},
"choicesType": "figure",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "Follow the car's distance from home during the drive, the hike, and the return drive.\n\nFrom \\(8\\) to \\(10\\) a.m., the car travels for \\(2\\) hours at \\(45\\) miles per hour, reaching a distance of \\(2\\cdot45=90\\) miles. During the next \\(3\\) hours the car stays at the trail, so its distance remains \\(90\\) miles until \\(1\\) p.m.\n\nThe return drive takes \\(90/60=1.5\\) hours. The graph must therefore fall from \\(90\\) miles at \\(1\\) p.m. to \\(0\\) at \\(2{:}30\\) p.m. Its downward segment is steeper than the outward segment because the return speed is greater.\n\nOnly graph \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\) has all these features. The flat part represents the parked car, even though Ling herself is hiking.",
"solutionSource": "Adapted from MAA official solutions",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://drive.usercontent.google.com/uc?id=1h0XYnHhGAtM4i3JxvGUgozPrlhZiYZQb&export=download",
